From ec87671307b2848c7a5723b731afd1c5a7c36d48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 19:19:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Save states: the GX front end's and gxcore's state, a drain,
 and a cut after a load

dol_aurora_gx_save_state drains the FIFO worker and returns the retail GX
front end's register model (CP/XF/BP, TMEM palettes, texture and copy
bindings, with the host-only resolver, FIFO copy and trace cleared) plus the
bytes of a command the guest has not finished writing, and the gxcore sink's
register state and cross-draw attribute cache. dol_aurora_gx_load_state puts
them back under this run's resolver: texture, palette and copy ranges are
resolved again against the restored guest memory, the texture cache is
emptied, and Smooth Motion's next game frame gets no in-between frames
(frame_interp::request_cut), as the frame before it is not the one it
follows. dol_aurora_gx_drain waits for the worker to finish what the guest
has written, so a load can replace guest memory the worker would otherwise
still be reading. dol_hle_callback_idle tells a host whether a memory card
completion callback is queued or running, when a state must not be taken.
